Input: {"question": "Where is Lincoln County High School located?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d00", "start": 0, "end": 129, "text": "Lincoln County High School (Kentucky) Lincoln County High School is a public secondary school located in Stanford, Kentucky, USA."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d00", "start": 130, "end": 353, "text": "It was opened in August 1974 for the 1974-1975 school year, after the consolidation of the local high schools of the towns of Lincoln County; Stanford, Crab Orchard, Hustonville, McKinney, and King Mountain area (Memorial)."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d00", "start": 354, "end": 442, "text": "In the 2016-2017 school year, 1027 students were enrolled at Lincoln County High School."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d00", "start": 443, "end": 594, "text": "An estimated 24,456 people live in Lincoln County as of 2017, so the students of Lincoln County High School represent 4.20% of the county's population."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d00", "start": 595, "end": 629, "text": "The mascot is the \"Patriot\", a man"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d01", "start": 0, "end": 132, "text": "Lincoln County High School (Kentucky) Lincoln County High School is a public secondary school located in Springfield, Illinois, USA."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d01", "start": 133, "end": 356, "text": "It was opened in August 1974 for the 1974-1975 school year, after the consolidation of the local high schools of the towns of Lincoln County; Stanford, Crab Orchard, Hustonville, McKinney, and King Mountain area (Memorial)."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d01", "start": 357, "end": 445, "text": "In the 2016-2017 school year, 1027 students were enrolled at Lincoln County High School."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d01", "start": 446, "end": 597, "text": "An estimated 24,456 people live in Lincoln County as of 2017, so the students of Lincoln County High School represent 4.20% of the county's population."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d01", "start": 598, "end": 633, "text": "The mascot is the \"Patriot\", a man."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d02", "start": 0, "end": 121, "text": "Lincoln County High School (West Virginia) Lincoln County High School is a Class AA high school in Hamlin, West Virginia."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d02", "start": 122, "end": 207, "text": "It was built between 2004 and 2006 and completed in time for the 2006/07 school year."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d02", "start": 208, "end": 432, "text": "Lincoln County High School was formed from four former high schools in the county: Guyan Valley High School in Pleasant View, Duval High School in Griffithsville, Hamlin High School in Hamlin, and Harts High School in Harts."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d02", "start": 433, "end": 550, "text": "The idea for consolidation had been tossed around the county for years, and protests and votes held the process back."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d02", "start": 551, "end": 590, "text": "Finally in 2000 due to low standardized"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d03", "start": 0, "end": 77, "text": "very student oriented , but my later years in high school were not the best ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0129-dccb931aa7ae:d03", "start": 78, "end": 147, "text": "New administration came and there were many issues within our roots ."}, "D